{{!-- A1's cover: the newest post, full-bleed, with the titling over the photo.

	{{> "home/hero" feed=feed}}

The lead is the first row of the shared query, which is to say the most recent post. That is the
signal, not a position in a fixture: the publication's own reverse-chronological order decides
what leads the cover, so publishing moves it.

The text colours are literal white rather than theme tokens — the scrim is dark in both Modes,
so nothing here can resolve against the page. That and the panel background below are the theme's
only non-token colours, and they are the same colour: #0c0a09 is rgb(12 10 9), the darkest stop of
the `hero-scrim` gradient in src/styles/main.css.

`h-[min(76vh,660px)]` is the design's height, and it is viewport-relative on purpose. Worth
knowing when reading a capture: a screenshot's window is as tall as the page, so 76vh always
resolves past the 660px cap there.

The panel carries the scrim's own darkest stop as a background. With a feature image the photo
covers it and it costs nothing; without one — Ghost lets a post publish with no image, and the
design has no drawing for that — the cover is a dark panel with the titling on it rather than
white text on the page background. --}}
{{#foreach feed limit="1"}}
	<section
		aria-labelledby="a1-lead"
		class="border-border relative border-b">
		<div class="relative h-[min(76vh,660px)] overflow-hidden bg-[#0c0a09]">
			{{#if feature_image}}
				<img
					src="{{img_url feature_image size="xxl"}}"
					{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
					fetchpriority="high"
					decoding="async"
					class="block h-full w-full object-cover">
			{{/if}}

			<div
				aria-hidden="true"
				class="hero-scrim absolute inset-0"></div>

			<div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 pb-14">
				<div class="container">
					<div class="flex items-center gap-3.5">
						{{#primary_tag}}
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="font-meta tracking-meta border-b border-white/50 text-xs text-white uppercase no-underline">{{name}}</a>
						{{/primary_tag}}

						<span class="font-meta tracking-meta text-xs text-white/72 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</span>
					</div>

					<h1
						id="a1-lead"
						class="font-display tracking-display mt-[18px] max-w-[20ch] text-[clamp(38px,5.4vw,72px)] leading-[1.03] font-medium text-balance text-white">
						<a
							href="{{url}}"
							class="text-white no-underline">{{title}}</a>
					</h1>

					<p class="text-lead mt-5 max-w-[56ch] leading-[1.5] text-pretty text-white/82">{{excerpt}}</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{{/foreach}}
